## SQ-PG-01a | server side: no PortalGunExitLift class or mixin; gun portals carry portalgun's own flag, unchanged
@group A
@commands #15 server side (rewritten 2026-11-14, was SQ-PG-01): boot; `grep -E "IPExitLiftMixin|PortalGunExitLift" logs/latest.log`; load a world copy with gun portals saved by the 2026-11-07 to 2026-11-13 jars (`adjustPositionAfterTeleport` 0b on some); `/data get entity @e[type=portalgun:custom_portal,limit=1,sort=nearest]`
@pass no mixin error; no `PortalGunExitLift` class or mixin named anywhere (the jar no longer has them; the client mixin is not applied on a dedicated server); old portals load without error, their saved flag unchanged and harmless
@fails `creativecompat.mixins.json` still lists `PortalGunExitLiftMixin`, or `CompatMixinPlugin` gate wrong
@from batches/r1115/p1_a1.qb
bootreject PortalGunExitLift|IPExitLiftMixin.*(fail|error)
shell grep -hE "IPExitLiftMixin|PortalGunExitLift" logs/latest.log | cut -c1-200 | head; echo "lines $(grep -cE 'IPExitLiftMixin|PortalGunExitLift' logs/latest.log)"; true
shell unzip -l mods/creativecompat-*.jar | grep -iE "ExitLift|portalgun" ; unzip -p mods/creativecompat-*.jar creativecompat.mixins.json | tr -d ' \n' | head -c 1500; echo; true
> forceload add 1280 1020 1320 1060
> fill 1290 -60 1040 1310 -50 1040 minecraft:stone
> pbot spawn pg 1300 -60 1030 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 4
> clear pg
> give pg portalgun:portal_gun 1
sleep 1
> execute as pg at @s run tp @s ~ ~ ~ -20 0
> zc3 shoot pg blue
sleep 2
> execute as pg at @s run tp @s ~ ~ ~ 20 0
> zc3 shoot pg orange
sleep 2
> zc3 portals
waitlog \[c3\] portals: \d+ 20
> execute as pg at @s run tp @s ~ ~ ~ 0 60
> zc3 shoot pg orange
sleep 2
> zc3 portals
waitlog \[c3\] portals: \d+ 20
reject \[c3\] error
look no ExitLift class/mixin in the jar or log; the flag values are portalgun's own (no recompute by colour/geometry); old-save half needs a fixture world (none kept)

## SQ-PG-01b | after the restart the saved gun portals keep the flag (read before the first beat)
@group client (scratch client, singleplayer, needs a window)
@commands #15 geometry: shoot gun portal pairs for wall to wall, wall to floor (exit on the floor) and floor to wall; walk (not jump) through each both ways; count `Adjusting Client Player Position` per pass in `logs/latest.log` (`Client Teleported` gives the portal); quit to title, reload the world, repeat once
@pass the adjust line appears only on passes that exit through a floor portal, never on a wall or ceiling exit; the same after the reload, also for portals placed before 2026-11-14
@fails sign or space of the test: `IPExitLiftMixin` reads `getContentDirection().y > 0.5` (destination space, not transformed again); a missing adjust line on floor exits means the redirect target (GETFIELD `adjustPositionAfterTeleport`) moved
@from batches/r1113/c3_a2.qb
> forceload add 1000 1000 1480 1080
> zc3 portals
waitlog \[c3\] portals: \d+ 20
expect \[c3\] portals: [1-9]
look the pg pair at x 1290-1310 z 1040 shows the same adjust values as the last SQ-PG-01a read (wall portal true, floor portal false); qa's spawn pair near x 0 z 10 also listed. Old-jar portals: not available (no pre-11-07 Compat jar kept), not judged

